# Frontend UI consistency (jobwright dashboard)

Any UI change in `frontend/` must keep the dashboard visually and structurally consistent.

## Before editing

1. Read peer screens that solve the same problem (sidebar vs drawer vs card vs table).
2. Check tokens in `frontend/src/index.css` (`:root`, `@layer components`).
3. Check shared primitives in `frontend/src/components/ui/` and domain components below.
4. Load [.cursor/skills/frontend-tasteful/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/frontend-tasteful/SKILL.md) for polish passes.

## Reuse order (do not skip)

1. **shadcn primitives** — `components/ui/` (`Button`, `Tabs`, `Badge`, `Input`, …). Use default variants; do not fork styles inline unless the pattern is promoted (see below).
2. **Domain layout components** — prefer these over ad-hoc flex/gap classes:
   - Sidebar: `NavItem`, `SidebarActionButton`, `CollapsedSidebarNav`
   - Job cards: `JobCardLayout`, `JobMetaPanel`, `MetaField`, `Chip`
   - Views: `ViewModeTabs` (Board/Table)
   - Stage color: `laneTone()` / `STAGE_TONE` from `lib/api.ts` (match Kanban column headers)
3. **CSS tokens** — add spacing/color to `:root` or `@layer components` (e.g. `--job-card-*`, `.job-card-*`), not scattered `text-[11px]`, `p-2.5`, `mt-0.5` mixes.

## New UI requests

- **Default:** extend an existing component or token. Briefly recommend the existing pattern before building something new.
- **If the user still wants a new control:** implement once as a **reusable** component (or token + class) in `components/`, wire all call sites, and note it in the PR/summary so future agents reuse it.
- **Do not** leave one-off markup/styles in `App.tsx` or page files when a shared primitive fits.

## Consistency rules (this project)

| Area | Standard |
|------|----------|
| Stage labels (sidebar) | ALL CAPS, `laneTone` color on label + count |
| Sidebar actions | Same row pattern as `NavItem` (icon + label expanded; icon-only collapsed) |
| Segmented controls | Default `TabsList` + `TabsTrigger` (rounded pill), not custom underline toggles |
| Job card rhythm | `JobCardLayout` slots + `--job-card-*` tokens; `text-sm` title, `text-xs` meta/chips |
| Chips / meta rows | `Chip` (`.job-card-chip`), `MetaField` (`.job-card-meta-row`) |
| Action buttons | `Button` from `ui/button` (`size="sm"`); `outline` for secondary, default for primary CTA |

## Examples

```tsx
// BAD — inline spacing/typography drift
<div className="space-y-2"><span className="text-[11px]">…</span></div>

// GOOD — shared layout + tokens
<JobCardBody><JobCardMeta><MetaField … /></JobCardMeta></JobCardBody>
```

```tsx
// BAD — custom header toggle
<TabsList className="rounded-none bg-transparent …">

// GOOD — project segmented control
<ViewModeTabs value={view} onChange={setView} />
```

```tsx
// BAD — text link posing as a button
<button className="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">Download</button>

// GOOD — shared Button primitive
<Button size="sm" variant="outline"><Download /> Download DOCX</Button>
```

## Do not

- Introduce hardcoded colors that duplicate lane/stage tokens.
- Add duplicate badge/chip/meta markup when `Chip` / `MetaField` / `NavItem` already fit.
- Use raw `<button>` with custom utility classes for actions; use `Button` (nav items and list rows are exceptions).
- Change behavior, data contracts, or accessibility to “fix” visuals.
